\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.1}{\ignorespaces Sketch of the LO and AS beam paths. The LO beam is obtained from the light transmitted by PR2. Some of this light is needed for control of the interferometer, so BHDBS1 is used to split the light. The LO beam is then directed towards the combining beam splitter BHDBS2 with BHDM1. Two lenses are needed to mode match the LO beam to the AS beam. THe AS beam is transmitted through the SRM, passes through the OFI, and is directed to BHDBS2 via OM0.\relax }}{10}{figure.caption.11}}
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:bhdforligochaptersketchoflodelivery}{{1.1}{10}{Sketch of the LO and AS beam paths. The LO beam is obtained from the light transmitted by PR2. Some of this light is needed for control of the interferometer, so BHDBS1 is used to split the light. The LO beam is then directed towards the combining beam splitter BHDBS2 with BHDM1. Two lenses are needed to mode match the LO beam to the AS beam. THe AS beam is transmitted through the SRM, passes through the OFI, and is directed to BHDBS2 via OM0.\relax }{figure.caption.11}{}}
